# @CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME@ API documentation

This is the API description. For usage and a description of the layers, refer
to:

```txt
$ man 1 dls
```

While not strictly necessary to understand the information flow in order to
build a plugin, it is briefly shown in the following diagram:

```txt
@FLOW_CHART_INCL@
```

## Quick Start

The following shows an extract from an example project and illustrates how to
write plugins for @CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME@.

PROTIP: The source code here contains hyperlinks. Use it to jump to the
documentation of a component.

### Building a new controller

Consider the header file:

```cpp
@EXAMPLE_CONTROLLER_HPP@
```
And its source file:

```cpp
@EXAMPLE_CONTROLLER_CPP@
```
To build and install it:

<!-- Figure out how to highlight this -->
```txt
@EXAMPLE_CONTROLLER_CMAKE@
```
### Building a new generator

Consider the header file:

```cpp
@EXAMPLE_GAIT_GENERATOR_HPP@
```
And its source file:

```cpp
@EXAMPLE_GAIT_GENERATOR_CPP@
```
To build and install it:

<!-- Figure out how to highlight this -->
```txt
@EXAMPLE_GAIT_GENERATOR_CMAKE@
```
